fter us-east, which is now on v2.3.0. us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry the rollback to v2.3.0 to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AvzwadgjuN7KnKppBtQYeL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01X3A4XhBAGSB6NP2yVU8gmW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Haunkc6JnZiLw5Vq5PxXf4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Deployment history: v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy; v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, leaving mixed versions); a second attempt completed the rollout. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure before re-releasing.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll retry with the same idempotency key, which ensures it is created at most once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SBbpBZtv9PGsMgkrF4s9v6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Deployment history: v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy; v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, leaving mixed versions); a second attempt completed the rollout. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure before re-releasing.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.18 \u2192 0.002).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, so I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. It had already been healthy in production, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving mixed versions. I checked the state and retried once, and the second attempt completed across us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. The first attempt timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident is open and has paged on-call. Its summary covers the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and the follow-ups.\n\nThe v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure still need investigation before v2.3.1 is re-released.", "type": "text"}]}]}